<% content_for :title, "Relapse Plans | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="toolbox-relapse-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="toolbox-relapse-hero">
    <div class="toolbox-relapse-hero-content">

      <p class="toolbox-relapse-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / TOOLBOX / RELAPSE PLANS
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>MAKE THE</span>
        <span>PLAN BEFORE</span>
        <span>YOU NEED IT.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="toolbox-relapse-intro">
        BECAUSE "I'LL FIGURE IT OUT<br>
        WHEN IT HAPPENS" IS A<br>
        SHITTY EMERGENCY PLAN.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- WHY -->
  <section class="relapse-section relapse-section-pink">

    <div class="relapse-section-number">
      01 / WHY HAVE A PLAN?
    </div>

    <div class="relapse-section-content">

      <h2>
        DON'T WAIT<br>
        FOR YOUR BRAIN<br>
        TO BE ON FIRE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The middle of a craving, mood episode, crisis, or fuck-it moment
        is not the ideal time to invent your entire recovery strategy.
      </p>

      <p>
        A relapse plan lets the version of you who can think clearly
        leave instructions for the version of you who might not be
        thinking so clearly later.
      </p>

      <div class="relapse-callout">
        <p>
          THE PLAN ISN'T PROOF<br>
          YOU'RE GOING TO RELAPSE.<br>
          IT'S PROOF YOU'RE PREPARING NOT TO.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- RELAPSE STARTS EARLIER -->
  <section class="relapse-section relapse-section-yellow">

    <div class="relapse-section-number">
      02 / THE SLIDE
    </div>

    <div class="relapse-section-content">

      <h2>
        RELAPSE CAN<br>
        START BEFORE<br>
        THE DRINK.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The substance use may be the obvious moment, but sometimes
        the slide starts earlier: routines disappear, isolation grows,
        thoughts change, cravings get romanticized, or recovery starts
        feeling less important.
      </p>

      <div class="relapse-flow">

        <p>STRESS / PAIN / MOOD CHANGE</p>
        <span>↓</span>

        <p>ISOLATION</p>
        <span>↓</span>

        <p>OLD THINKING COMES BACK</p>
        <span>↓</span>

        <p>ROMANTICIZING</p>
        <span>↓</span>

        <p>BARGAINING</p>
        <span>↓</span>

        <p>OPPORTUNITY</p>
        <span>↓</span>

        <p>USE</p>

      </div>

      <p>
        Your pattern may look completely different.
        That's the point of writing down <strong>your</strong> pattern.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- WARNING SIGNS -->
  <section class="relapse-section relapse-section-purple">

    <div class="relapse-section-number">
      03 / WARNING SIGNS
    </div>

    <div class="relapse-section-content">

      <h2>
        KNOW YOUR<br>
        RED FUCKING<br>
        FLAGS.
      </h2>

      <p>
        What tends to change before you're in real trouble?
      </p>

      <div class="relapse-checklist">

        <div>
          <span>□</span>
          <p>I'm isolating more.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>□</span>
          <p>I'm skipping recovery routines or support.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>□</span>
          <p>I'm romanticizing drinking or using.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>□</span>
          <p>I'm thinking, "Maybe I can handle it now."</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>□</span>
          <p>I'm hiding what I'm thinking from people who support me.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>□</span>
          <p>My sleep is changing significantly.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>□</span>
          <p>My mood is shifting.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>□</span>
          <p>I'm getting more impulsive.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>□</span>
          <p>I'm putting myself near people, places, or situations connected to using.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="relapse-callout">
        <p>
          DON'T WAIT UNTIL EVERY RED FLAG<br>
          IS WAVING AT THE SAME FUCKING TIME.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- TRIGGERS -->
  <section class="relapse-section relapse-section-black">

    <div class="relapse-section-number">
      04 / TRIGGERS
    </div>

    <div class="relapse-section-content">

      <h2>
        WHAT MAKES<br>
        YOU WANT<br>
        OUT?
      </h2>

      <p>
        A trigger doesn't force you to use.
        It tells you that your risk just changed.
      </p>

      <div class="relapse-plan-grid">

        <div>
          <p class="relapse-label">TRIGGER</p>
          <p>What happened?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="relapse-label">URGE</p>
          <p>What do I suddenly want to do?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="relapse-label">NEED</p>
          <p>What am I actually trying to get?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="relapse-label">MOVE</p>
          <p>What can I do instead?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Pain. Depression. Mania. Anger. Loneliness. Shame.
        Boredom. Conflict. Celebration. Money. Certain people.
        Certain places.
      </p>

      <p>
        Get specific. "Stress" is useful.
        "After I fight with somebody and feel trapped" is more useful.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- CRAVING -->
  <section class="relapse-section relapse-section-pink">

    <div class="relapse-section-number">
      05 / WHEN THE CRAVING HITS
    </div>

    <div class="relapse-section-content">

      <h2>
        DO NOT<br>
        FUCKING<br>
        NEGOTIATE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        A craving loves a debate.
      </p>

      <p>
        "Maybe just one." "Maybe this time is different."
        "Maybe I deserve it." "Maybe nobody needs to know."
      </p>

      <p>
        Your plan should require as little decision-making as possible.
      </p>

      <div class="relapse-action-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Leave the situation if alcohol or substances are available.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Contact somebody from your support system.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Eat something. Drink water. Deal with immediate physical needs.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Change locations.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>Delay the decision. You do not need to decide "forever" right now.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <p>Read your reasons for staying sober.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>07</span>
          <p>Keep putting time between the urge and the action.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PLAY THE TAPE -->
  <section class="relapse-section relapse-section-yellow">

    <div class="relapse-section-number">
      06 / PLAY THE WHOLE TAPE
    </div>

    <div class="relapse-section-content">

      <h2>
        DON'T STOP<br>
        THE MOVIE AT<br>
        THE GOOD PART.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The craving usually shows you the beginning:
        relief, numbness, excitement, escape.
      </p>

      <p>
        Keep going.
      </p>

      <div class="relapse-tape">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>What happens during the first hour?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>What usually happens after that?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>What happens to my judgment?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>What happens to my relationships?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>What consequences have happened before?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <p>How do I feel the next morning?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="relapse-callout">
        <p>
          REMEMBER THE WHOLE FUCKING STORY.<br>
          NOT JUST THE FIRST DRINK.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PEOPLE -->
  <section class="relapse-section relapse-section-purple">

    <div class="relapse-section-number">
      07 / PEOPLE
    </div>

    <div class="relapse-section-content">

      <h2>
        WHO NEEDS<br>
        TO FUCKING<br>
        KNOW?
      </h2>

      <p>
        Decide who you're contacting before you're trying to convince
        yourself that contacting nobody is a brilliant idea.
      </p>

      <div class="relapse-contact-grid">

        <div>
          <p class="relapse-label">PERSON 01</p>
          <p>Someone I can call when I'm craving.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="relapse-label">PERSON 02</p>
          <p>Someone who understands my recovery.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="relapse-label">PERSON 03</p>
          <p>Someone who can physically be with me if I need support.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="relapse-label">PROFESSIONAL</p>
          <p>A therapist, treatment provider, doctor, or other professional support.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Put actual names and contact information in your personal plan.
        "I'll call someone" is a lot less useful than knowing exactly who.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENVIRONMENT -->
  <section class="relapse-section relapse-section-black">

    <div class="relapse-section-number">
      08 / ENVIRONMENT
    </div>

    <div class="relapse-section-content">

      <h2>
        MAKE RELAPSE<br>
        MORE FUCKING<br>
        INCONVENIENT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Willpower is not the only tool available to you.
        Change the environment.
      </p>

      <div class="relapse-action-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Remove alcohol or substances from your space.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Avoid high-risk places when you're struggling.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Don't carry more money than you need if spending increases your risk.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Change the route if a familiar stop is part of the old routine.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>Don't intentionally put yourself next to the thing you're trying not to do.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="relapse-callout">
        <p>
          YOU DON'T GET EXTRA POINTS<br>
          FOR MAKING SOBRIETY HARDER.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- BIPOLAR -->
  <section class="relapse-section relapse-section-pink">

    <div class="relapse-section-number">
      09 / BIPOLAR + RELAPSE
    </div>

    <div class="relapse-section-content">

      <h2>
        WATCH THE<br>
        MOOD<br>
        SHIFTS.
      </h2>

      <p>
        If bipolar symptoms and substance use interact for you,
        changes in mood may also change relapse risk.
      </p>

      <p>
        Depression may increase the desire to escape or numb.
        Elevated or manic states may increase impulsivity,
        confidence, risk-taking, or the feeling that consequences
        don't fucking apply right now.
      </p>

      <div class="relapse-action-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Watch significant changes in sleep.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Notice unusual increases in energy or impulsivity.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Notice worsening depression or hopelessness.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Use your psychiatric and recovery supports early when symptoms change.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        A relapse plan can sit alongside your bipolar treatment plan.
        It doesn't replace medical or psychiatric care.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- THE PLAN -->
  <section class="relapse-section relapse-section-yellow">

    <div class="relapse-section-number">
      10 / WRITE YOUR PLAN
    </div>

    <div class="relapse-section-content">

      <h2>
        PUT IT<br>
        ON FUCKING<br>
        PAPER.
      </h2>

      <div class="relapse-workbook">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>MY WARNING SIGNS</h3>
          <p>What changes before I'm in trouble?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>MY TRIGGERS</h3>
          <p>What situations, feelings, or states increase my risk?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>MY REASONS</h3>
          <p>What am I protecting by staying sober?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>MY PEOPLE</h3>
          <p>Who am I contacting before I make a decision?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <h3>MY SAFE PLACES</h3>
          <p>Where can I go where using is less likely?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <h3>MY FIRST MOVE</h3>
          <p>What exactly will I do when I realize I'm at risk?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- IF A LAPSE HAPPENS -->
  <section class="relapse-section relapse-section-purple">

    <div class="relapse-section-number">
      11 / IF YOU USE
    </div>

    <div class="relapse-section-content">

      <h2>
        STOP THE<br>
        FUCK-IT<br>
        SPIRAL.
      </h2>

      <p>
        A lapse does not require turning one episode of use into
        a week, month, or complete abandonment of recovery.
      </p>

      <div class="relapse-before-after">

        <div>
          <p class="relapse-label">THE SPIRAL</p>
          <p>I ALREADY FUCKED UP, SO FUCK IT.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="relapse-label">THE MOVE</p>
          <p>I USED. WHAT DO I NEED TO DO NEXT?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="relapse-action-list">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Get somewhere physically safe.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>Tell somebody instead of hiding it.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Get medical help if there's any concern about overdose, withdrawal, or your immediate safety.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Remove access to more alcohol or substances.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>Look at what happened before the lapse.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <p>Update the fucking plan.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="relapse-ending">

    <p class="relapse-ending-small">
      DON'T MAKE THE PLAN IN THE MIDDLE OF THE FUCKING EMERGENCY.
    </p>

    <h2>
      KNOW THE SIGNS.<br>
      KNOW THE MOVE.<br>
      KNOW YOUR PEOPLE.
    </h2>

    <p>
      Your plan doesn't have to be perfect.
      It needs to be clear enough that you can use it when your brain
      starts trying to renegotiate everything.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO TOOLBOX",
        toolbox_path,
        class: "relapse-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>